        "fr-extract.jsonl": [
            {
                "entry_id": "2ce0e44e-3579-329a-9a42-a8948f13e24b",
                "word": "longanimité",
                "pos": "noun",
                "lang_code": "fr",
                "forms": [
                    {
                        "form_id": "e09171da-839a-4981-823a-d48242b8c6d6",
                        "entry_id": "2ce0e44e-3579-329a-9a42-a8948f13e24b",
                        "tags": [
                            "plural"
                        ],
                        "form": "longanimités"
                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "3f2f5b29-4035-3e6e-8d96-118b95531bac",
                        "entry_id": "2ce0e44e-3579-329a-9a42-a8948f13e24b",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Patience avec laquelle un être puissant et bon endure les fautes, les insultes qu’il pourrait punir."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "literary"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "f268f7ee-43b5-467d-88c8-3ae399932f12",
                                "sense_id": "3f2f5b29-4035-3e6e-8d96-118b95531bac",
                                "text": "L’adresse et la longanimité de ces jeunes gens du grand monde finiraient par triompher de mon peu d’expérience, se dit-il; il faut partir et mettre un terme à tout ceci."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "8c7bc57a-f7cf-48dc-9e86-0091c9b00544",
                                "sense_id": "3f2f5b29-4035-3e6e-8d96-118b95531bac",
                                "text": "Il fallut à M. de Morvelle toute la longanimité d’un candidat pour ne rien laisser voir de l’humeur que lui causait cette chicane."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "9d821cc8-b667-412f-89b4-23a2854ab3df",
                                "sense_id": "3f2f5b29-4035-3e6e-8d96-118b95531bac",
                                "text": "Hélas ! Messieurs, le Dieu de nos pères, qui devait armer d’un papier vengeur la main de l’électeur, s’est montré d’une longanimité, d’une indifférence sans pareille."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "770d6298-fe1d-4e7d-b719-78e149ce9474",
                                "sense_id": "3f2f5b29-4035-3e6e-8d96-118b95531bac",
                                "text": "Et ils s’en retournent dans leur pays, admirant la longanimité d’Allah qui permet à une race aussi dévergondée d’opprimer les croyants, mais consolés par la certitude qu’au jugement dernier les infidèles n’échapperont pas à leur juste châtiment, qu’ils seront la proie de Chaïtân et brûleront éternellement en enfer."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "aa73ec6d-9e9e-402e-8800-2cfbdec506a7",
                                "sense_id": "3f2f5b29-4035-3e6e-8d96-118b95531bac",
                                "text": "On se demande pourquoi Mme Pardoux a l’air si royal : c’est sa politesse et sa bonté, sa longanimité, la qualité supérieure de son hypocrisie, la fleur de son amabilité sans danger d’être dupe, qui lui confère tant de distinction."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "2ffd176a-95e7-4bf1-8d5a-49743b40f34d",
                        "source_entry_id": "2ce0e44e-3579-329a-9a42-a8948f13e24b",
                        "source_sense_id": "3f2f5b29-4035-3e6e-8d96-118b95531bac",
                        "source_sense_description": "Patience endurant les fautes",
                        "target_lang_word": "Langmut",
                        "target_lang_code": "de",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "Langmut",
                                "target_lang_code": "de",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "92fd7b78-a9a3-3d9b-8296-dddc1647566c",
                                        "entry_id": "75f15cbf-3bec-38b1-9dbb-63dd3999d3c5",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "große Geduld, Gelassenheit, Zurückhaltung"
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "literary"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "a2b9a0f7-5c43-4a9b-85ba-a7d0ee305309",
                                                "sense_id": "92fd7b78-a9a3-3d9b-8296-dddc1647566c",
                                                "text": "Mit Langmut erduldete er die Debatte."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "a295413b-f7ed-4035-8953-16d2862b2626",
                                                "sense_id": "92fd7b78-a9a3-3d9b-8296-dddc1647566c",
                                                "text": "Seine Langmut, sich mit dem nörgelnden Kind zu beschäftigen, war bewundernswert."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "dc10ac1c-151b-4543-a08f-00435db1197e",
                                                "sense_id": "92fd7b78-a9a3-3d9b-8296-dddc1647566c",
                                                "text": "Man muß schon eine Menge Langmut aufbringen, um diesen Film zu Ende zu sehen."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "6b5ab2d8-d800-440d-8232-b4ab83bfe47c",
                                                "sense_id": "92fd7b78-a9a3-3d9b-8296-dddc1647566c",
                                                "text": "Pekings Langmut mit seinem nervigen Verbündeten in Nordkorea könnte Grenzen haben."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "dea747cf-4950-4232-a481-bde0e4703523",
                                                "sense_id": "92fd7b78-a9a3-3d9b-8296-dddc1647566c",
                                                "text": "„Das Spiel absolvierte sie in seltsamer Langmut.“"
                                            }
                                        ],
                                        "sense_index_json": "\"1\""
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "73a62841-c372-4c7b-bf33-b409c8a9b65d",
                        "source_entry_id": "2ce0e44e-3579-329a-9a42-a8948f13e24b",
                        "source_sense_id": "3f2f5b29-4035-3e6e-8d96-118b95531bac",
                        "source_sense_description": "Patience endurant les fautes",
                        "target_lang_word": "forbearance",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "forbearance",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "7e6c3065-6c26-3634-8dd7-596a7d604011",
                                        "entry_id": "09877578-a383-3b4e-9879-599ce8f2e671",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Patient self-control; restraint and tolerance under provocation."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "37105e3f-82e8-40db-b0ed-fd240e00a1f5",
                                                "sense_id": "7e6c3065-6c26-3634-8dd7-596a7d604011",
                                                "text": "Though I would give no information, he discovered, through some of the other servants, both her place of residence, and the existence of the child. Still he didn’t molest her; for which forbearance she might thank his aversion, I suppose."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "85d26ad3-be57-446c-b129-858fe3cb4526",
                                                "sense_id": "7e6c3065-6c26-3634-8dd7-596a7d604011",
                                                "text": "I WOULD HAVE been nine or ten when my mother chased me up a thorn tree with a ceremonial hippo-hide whip. What my crime was, I forget. My mother was, and remains, a woman of exceptional forbearance. I must have done something so obnoxious as to beggar belief."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "29bb35f2-3d74-3cec-a01a-3dc8a808a7ce",
                                        "entry_id": "09877578-a383-3b4e-9879-599ce8f2e671",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A refraining from the enforcement of something (as a debt, right, or obligation) that is due."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": []
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "9d9a51d1-478e-4860-9d46-b6350eb0f4af",
                        "source_entry_id": "2ce0e44e-3579-329a-9a42-a8948f13e24b",
                        "source_sense_id": "3f2f5b29-4035-3e6e-8d96-118b95531bac",
                        "source_sense_description": "Patience endurant les fautes",
                        "target_lang_word": "longanimity",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "longanimity",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "a4cdc872-383e-3a5d-b273-7c20aa511869",
                                        "entry_id": "e4581bd7-fe6f-35d4-916d-dd9926bc8cd2",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Patience or tolerance in the face of adversity; forbearance, long-suffering."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "archaic",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "3bd5c3b0-6ef2-4e51-ba61-46879c6e72b6",
                                                "sense_id": "a4cdc872-383e-3a5d-b273-7c20aa511869",
                                                "text": "It had overcome the patience of Job, as it did the meekness of Moses, and would surely have mastered any, but the longanimity, and lasting sufferance of God [...]."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "a2f55b55-4d00-4759-bfca-0b9ffe1a651b",
                        "source_entry_id": "2ce0e44e-3579-329a-9a42-a8948f13e24b",
                        "source_sense_id": "3f2f5b29-4035-3e6e-8d96-118b95531bac",
                        "source_sense_description": "Patience endurant les fautes",
                        "target_lang_word": "fortitude",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "fortitude",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "3d9746e7-f0b4-3bd3-88ab-0f1959a18f3c",
                                        "entry_id": "bce157a7-29fe-3dcc-8100-46ff55721e8a",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Mental or emotional strength that enables courage in the face of adversity."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "b61d6bb1-230f-43e8-96de-694bfc123407",
                                                "sense_id": "3d9746e7-f0b4-3bd3-88ab-0f1959a18f3c",
                                                "text": "I am able now (me thinkes) / (Out of a Fortitude of Soule, I feele) / To endure more Miſeries, […]"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "89808fbf-5a34-48bf-9fa8-61d589721853",
                                                "sense_id": "3d9746e7-f0b4-3bd3-88ab-0f1959a18f3c",
                                                "text": "I shall soon have need for all my fortitude, as I am on the point of separation from my own daughter."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "43f66603-68f1-4bec-9cff-662e9c9c1455",
                                                "sense_id": "3d9746e7-f0b4-3bd3-88ab-0f1959a18f3c",
                                                "text": "She [the ship] may be saved by your efforts, by your resource and fortitude bearing up against the heavy weight of guilt and failure."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "447771ce-6bcc-4596-9e55-657d4a8dc72c",
                                                "sense_id": "3d9746e7-f0b4-3bd3-88ab-0f1959a18f3c",
                                                "text": "Mitt Romney […] charges that [Barack] Obama is an appeaser who apologizes for America, lacks fortitude and is \"tentative, indecisive, timid and nuanced.\""
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "3700f0aa-47f1-4a49-8ca8-cb71e9bf549d",
                                                "sense_id": "3d9746e7-f0b4-3bd3-88ab-0f1959a18f3c",
                                                "text": "The proper fans might also expend time—about twenty hours—trying to visit every Tube station as quickly as possible. […] But to visit every station in record time—which people have been attempting since at least 1960—requires real fortitude. You must get up before dawn, you must drink or eat almost nothing, so niggardly is the Underground with toilet provision."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "bf7d253d-d4a0-353f-9d5d-85438bacc39c",
                                        "entry_id": "bce157a7-29fe-3dcc-8100-46ff55721e8a",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Physical strength."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "archaic",
                                            "countable",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "f890a459-b9ac-4b36-94c9-2bfbe8927190",
                                                "sense_id": "bf7d253d-d4a0-353f-9d5d-85438bacc39c",
                                                "text": "The Turke with moſt mighty preparation makes for Cipres. Othello, the fortitude of the place, is beſt knowne to you, […]"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "3b1a1867-51d7-4c7e-93e6-0297d98dfcad",
                                                "sense_id": "bf7d253d-d4a0-353f-9d5d-85438bacc39c",
                                                "text": "Hey day! VVhat are all the VVomen of my Family abroad? Is not my Wife come home? Nor my Siſter, nor my Daughter? […] Mercy on us, what can be the meaning of it? Sure the Moon is in all her Fortitudes; […]"
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "c16e5d9f-7594-47f2-848c-55ec80c358f0",
                        "source_entry_id": "2ce0e44e-3579-329a-9a42-a8948f13e24b",
